      "why": "iterative is the smallest-area family (shared datapath, no pipeline registers). It is the only candidate that can plausibly hit the 1 MSPS throughput constraint with minimal LUT+FF, since its throughput is Fmax/latency and its latency (N+3) is short for small N. I focus data_width 8-12 and n_iter 8-14 because the error constraint (<= 2^-10) is tight for low width/iter; the search will find the minimal (W, N) pair that satisfies max_abs_err while keeping area low. angle_guard and frac_guard are kept narrow (small non-negative) to avoid inflating the atan-LUT and datapath width, which directly hurts the area objective."
